{
  "id": "19197",
  "key": "SFCC-746",
  "summary": "Navigation – PWA Kit & Contentful",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, I want to see a consistent headline navigation on every page, so that I can access top-level site categories and key account actions regardless of where I am on the site.\n\n**As a** Site Merchandiser, I want to manage the top-level navigation items in Contentful, so that the nav structure can be updated per storefront without a code deployment.\n\n----\n\nThis is a **Contentful component and PWA Kit story**. It covers the Contentful content type and the build of the `Navigation` React component in the PWA Kit storefront — the headline nav bar that renders on every page across all storefronts and devices.\n\nThe `Navigation` component was initially built as part of SFCC-52, which focused on the visual structure and placement of the headline nav items. That story was in build before the new component approach was developed. This story supersedes the navigation portion of SFCC-52 and defines the full `Navigation` component at the headline level.\n\nTop-level nav items, their ordering, and storefront visibility are managed in Contentful using the category ID to key back to the SFCC category taxonomy in BM. The PWA Kit component consumes the Contentful entries to render the headline nav bar. Mega menu behaviour on desktop is covered in SFCC-96. Mobile hamburger and drill-down behaviour is also covered in SFCC-96.\n\nThe following are explicitly out of scope: hover/focus/active visual states (defined in UI kit).\n\n**Motion Design:** [https://zimmermann-handover-ja2o39l78-song-ddp-anz.vercel.app/#templates%2Fmain](https://zimmermann-handover-ja2o39l78-song-ddp-anz.vercel.app/#templates%2Fmain) should be followed for scroll behaviour \n\n**UI Kit:** [https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026?node-id=2083-53877](https://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann*Design*System*2026)  \n\n**Desktop:** \n\n![\"image-20260831-033603.png\"](image-20260831-033603.png)",
