          "field": "Dependency",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "from_string": "SFCC-28 (Base Category Setup) — top-level category taxonomy must be configured in BM before nav items can be wired up. SFCC-28 is already deployed to UAT; confirm categories are stable before build begins.\nSFCC-96 (Desktop Mega Menu) and SFCC-97 (Mobile Hamburger and Drill-Down) — Navigation component must be in place before these stories can be built on top of it.\nSFCC-93 (Logo Scroll Behaviour) — confirm whether nav and logo scroll behaviour are tied to the same motion design decision. AC16 is blocked until confirmed.\n@Jersey Perez Jr: This story supersedes the navigation portion of SFCC-52 — confirm what has already been built to avoid rework before picking up.\n\nOpen Items:\n@Design team: Confirm exact scroll animation behaviour for the nav on scroll — does it stick only, or does it also shrink or change appearance? Consistent across all page templates? (AC16).\n@Zimmermann / Business: Confirm whether a SALE nav item is required. If so, does it appear permanently or only during sale periods? If conditional, what drives its visibility — BM configuration, Contentful, or a feature flag? SFCC-28 may need to be updated accordingly.\n@Zimmermann / Business: Confirm whether Back in Boutique should appear as a top-level headline nav item, consistent with how it is referenced in SFCC-96 and SFCC-97. If so, confirm whether it triggers a mega menu or links directly to a page.\n@Design team / Jersey Perez Jr: Confirm Z.IMMERSE link destination — is this an SFCC-managed page or a Contentful landing page?\n@Design team / Jersey Perez Jr: Confirm Account icon behaviour when shopper is unauthenticated — to be resolved in the Account feature story.",
