      "id": "18141",
      "key": "SFCC-96",
      "summary": "Expanded Navigation - PWA Kit and Contentful",
      "description": "As a Shopper, I want to see a mega menu appear when I hover over or click a top-level navigation category on desktop, so that I can quickly browse subcategories and editorial content without leaving the current page.\nAs a Site Merchandiser, I want to manage the mega menu content in Contentful, so that subcategory links, editorial links, and campaign imagery can be updated per storefront without a code deployment.\n_\nThis story covers both the Contentful content model and the PWA Kit component build for the expanded desktop navigation (mega menu). The component has been partially built — this story formalises the Contentful integration, editorial content slots, and completes the remaining behaviour.\nWhat the mega menu displays:\nOn hover or click of a top-level nav item, a full-width panel opens below the header containing two areas:\nLeft column\n — subcategory links (e.g. DRESSES, BAGS, TAILORING) followed by editorial links (e.g. FALL 2026, VIEW ALL)\nRight area\n — a large campaign image\nA CLOSE control is available top-right to dismiss the panel.\nAll mega menu content — subcategory links, editorial links, campaign imagery, and their ordering — is managed in Contentful. This allows the nav structure to include editorial destinations (e.g. campaign or collection pages) alongside standard category links, without requiring a code change. Content can vary per storefront.\nUI Kit:\n \nhttps://www.figma.com/design/wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm/Zimmermann_Design_System_2026?node-id=2083-53877&p=f&t=GBRCVRrX3RCrbURg-0\n \nDesigns:\n \nhttps://www.figma.com/design/QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs/Zimmermann_Designs?node-id=3051-37191&t=7MDyoGWpJfsFAZI3-0\n \nProduct Category Taxonomy:\n \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/380043284/Product+Category+Taxonomy\n \nNew / Collections: Seasonal \nReference Images (Figma is leading):\nDesktop: ",
      "status": {
        "name": "Ready For Review",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
