{"result":"{
  "id": "18142",
  "key": "SFCC-97",
  "summary": "Expanded Navigation (Mobile) - PWA Kit Component",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper,\n\n**I want** to open a navigation menu from a hamburger icon on mobile and drill down through headings to reach subcategories,\n\n**so that** I can find and navigate to the right section of the site without needing a full desktop layout.\n\n----\n\n**Reference Image (Figma is leading):**\n\n\n![\"image-20260726-230231.png\"](image-20260726-230231.png)\n\n**Context:**\n\nOn mobile, the global header collapses the navigation into a hamburger menu icon. Tapping it opens a full navigation panel. Rather than showing all levels at once, the navigation uses a drill-down pattern — the shopper taps a top-level heading to reveal its subcategories, and can continue navigating deeper into the hierarchy. A back control allows them to return to the previous level.\n\nKey behaviours:\n\n- Tapping the hamburger icon opens the mobile navigation panel\n- The panel displays top-level navigation categories\n- Tapping a category that has subcategories drills into that category, replacing the top-level view with the subcategory list\n- A back control is visible at the top of the panel to return to the previous level\n- Z.Immerse functions as a direct link and does not drill down\n- The 'Back in Boutique' category is included in the nav\n- Tapping a destination link closes the panel and navigates to the relevant page\n- Nav items are CMS-managed; adding or removing items does not require a code change\n\nThis story is design-dependent — the panel layout, animation, and drill-down transition behaviour must come from the Figma spec before implementation begins.",
